Metric-based anomaly detection and root cause analysis (RCA) for microservice systems have
been extensively studied in recent years [33, 40, 42, 43, 45, 47, 58, 59, 72, 73, 75]. Given a set
of metrics data, anomaly detection techniques aim to detect whether there exist anomalies and
consequently, failures within the microservice system [33, 42]. If a failure is detected, the RCA
module is then triggered to locate the root cause of the failure [40, 42, 43]. The RCA module aims
to address two fundamental questions: (1) which services are the root causes,
